Aegean Iconography, Aegis 18 (2020), pp. 223–252.”  
- **URL**: 
https://www.academia.edu/43416584/_2020_A_G_Vlachopoulos_The_Ring_of_Nestor_and_
the_quest_for_authenticity_in_F_Blakolmer_ed_Current_Approaches_and_New_Perspect
ives_in_Aegean_Iconography_Aegis_18_2020_pp_223_252  
- **发布方/作者**: Andreas G. Vlachopoulos；原载于 Aegis 
18（印刷/正规学术出版）；Academia.edu 为在线自存档平台  
- **日期**: 2020  
- **来源类型**: 学术期刊/论文集论文（通过 Academia.edu 访问的自存档版本）  
- **触发它的查询语句**: `"The Ring of Nestor gold signet-ring Evans JHS"`  
- **与检索目标的相关性**:  
  - 研究专门聚焦于 “so-called Ring of Nestor (CMS VI, no. 277)” 
的真伪问题，同时总结 20 世纪以来的学界讨论。  
  - 摘要中有明确的 Aegean Bronze Age 语境描述：  
    > “... these unique signet rings of the first centuries of the Late Bronze 
Age (16th–15th century BC).”  
  - 虽然这篇文章并非 
“核心一手发现文献”，但却是高水准的现代综述，可用来补充文化时期（Late Bronze Age,
Aegean / Creto-Mycenaean）和尺寸等细节。  
- **可见正文 / 忠实摘录**（来自页面 `raw_content` 摘要）：  
  > “The many years of research that led to the present paper on the so-called 
Ring of Nestor (CMS VI, nο. 277), with the documentation of its authenticity, 
have offered me the opportunity to discuss the cases of erroneous 
identifications of some Creto-Mycenaean gold rings as fakes. This tendency, 
underpinned by the obscure – even legendary – circumstances in which these rings
were found, not only the Ring of Nestor but also the Ring of Minos, has been 
reassessed completely in favour of their authenticity. This revision has been 
significantly reinforced by recent finds of iconographic subjects of comparable 
resonance (wall-paintings, gold rings, figurines, ivories, and so on), as well 
as by more thorough study of the techniques and craftsmanship of these unique 
signet rings of the first centuries of the Late Bronze Age (16th-15th century 
BC). The key pictorial unit of the Ring of Nestor examined in this paper is 
Evans’s ‘watch-dog’ or ‘dragon’, namely the guardian of the old ‘tree of the 
world’, whose branches host the most populous scene in Aegean glyptic art.”  

  虽然这段没有逐字写出 “gold signet ring from Boeotia”，但清楚表明：  
  - Ring of Nestor 被视为 “Creto-Mycenaean gold ring”；  
  - 属于 “unique signet rings ... of the Late Bronze Age (16th–15th century 
BC)”；  
  - 置于 Aegean glyptic 及图像学背景。

